In <57700015@uxa.cso.uiuc.edu> ews00461@uxa.cso.uiuc.edu writes:


>What is a good plan to avoid dying of starvation (IMHO, by far
>the most frustrating way to die.) ?

I recently posed the same question, and got some good advice
spoilers:

 Eat everything you can immediately(the non poisoned stuff).  Tainting
only affects stuff that's been sitting around for a while(20 or so turns?)
I usually play a barbarian, so I don't have any trouble with being poisoned,
but there are ways to gain poison resistance.(try eating some usually
poisonous things bees,brn puddings, but make sure you have some healing
stuff available.)
 One other hint, you might want to keep yourself stridently aligned
for those weak moments in life, if you know what I mean.

>Do super advanced players still find themselves equally prone
>to dying from starvation, sickness from eating tainted meat, etc...

 Play a while using the above hints, and it won't be near the problem.
Usually, I have too much food around level 8, and have to drop some.

>The teleport command (on the Mac, under the Move menu), must have
>some function eventually.  When does one gain this ability ?  Can you
>teleport to a specific level ?

 Yes, teleporting at will is a later option.  I think wizards get
it at a higher level, and eating a tengu gives it to you also.

>What is everyone's favorite type of character (ie wizard, priest,
>tourist, etc...)  Why ?

  It's hard to beat that early poison resistance and the speed you get
at level 7 when you play a barbarian.  Plus, you always get great str,dex,
and con.  They're vital to being able to romp around at will.  The str
lets you carry a lot more stuff, also.
  
